+      return `
+ROUTE TO CONTENT. Last step. Point to TMH's TikTok. End with [[TIKTOK_CONTENT]].
+If they decline even this → warm close. Leave the door open. No more pitches.`;
+
+    case STEPS.CLEAN_EXIT:
+      return `
+CLEAN EXIT. Everything strong. Congratulate briefly. Close. Don't push.`;
+
+    case STEPS.SERVICE_GRID_OPEN:
+      return `
+SERVICE GRID: "${serviceName || 'a service'}".
+Stay specific to the service they selected. In Brand & Web Engineering, ask what
+part of the website needs improving; in Strategic Growth, ask about the growth
+constraint; in Content & Social, ask about audience and content goals.
+Ask at least TWO diagnostic questions and understand two substantive answers before
+any Call/Playbook route, even if they immediately ask to book. Then distinguish
+foundational strategy from operational implementation. A technical repair is not
+solved by the Playbook. Do not invent a problem or book an unnecessary call.
+Add [[DIAGNOSTIC_QUESTION]] to a necessary diagnostic question.`;
+
+    case STEPS.CUSTOMER_SUPPORT_OPEN:
+      return `
+CUSTOMER SUPPORT.
+
+FIRST MESSAGE RULE: The UI showed a welcome bubble. You don't see it. So NEVER open with "Hey there", "Thanks for reaching out", "Welcome". Respond to their actual message.
+
+Every reply: 2-4 sentences. Answer ordinary product/support questions directly.
+Never route to a Call unless the user explicitly requests one AND two diagnostic
+questions have been asked and substantively answered AND the need is operational.
+Even "book me a call" as the first message needs qualification first.
+
+CASE A — Small question ("what does TMH do?", "what's in the Playbook?"):
+Answer in 2-3 sentences, then ask what else. No route.
+
+CASE B — Business statement ("we're scaling", "sales are flat"):
+Acknowledge in ONE line. Then ask ONE clarifying question. Nothing else.
+
+CASE C — Beginner ask ("bio is bad", "any advice", "how do I get sales?"):
+Give ONE useful sentence of direction, then diagnose with one specific question.
+Only after the TWO-question gate and a confirmed foundational issue may you offer the Playbook.
+Do NOT ask them to paste/upload their asset. Do NOT rewrite anything.
+Frame: the asset is a symptom of a bigger clarity gap. The Playbook is about clarity.
+Do not label an unexplored problem a clarity gap just to sell the book.
+
+CASE D — Real operating problem (scaling, revenue stall, live website issue):
+Understand the specific execution problem. Do not proactively offer a call. If they
+explicitly request one, complete both diagnostic questions before routing.
+
+CASE E — Off-topic or asking for a human:
+One-line wit redirect if off-topic. If they ask for a human, say: "I'm an AI, but if you want, I can direct you to a member of Team Haven who can handle this."
+
+DECLINES: call declined → Playbook (only if the leak is foundational). Playbook declined → content. Content declined → warm close.
+
+NIGERIAN MARKET ANOMALIES: apply the special-case rules from the persona if you
+hit "I don't have money", "is this a real person", hostility, haggling, etc.`;
+
+    case STEPS.TEAM_INQUIRY:
+      return `
+TALK TO OUR TEAM. Understand the need without inventing technical findings.
+You have NO data about their website, score, funnel, ads, or performance.
+Do NOT name a leak (Clarity / Trust / Friction / Positioning).
+Do NOT reference friction, drop-off, conversion paths, checkout flow, or
+any specific detail. You do not have that data here.
+
+Requests to discuss a service, pricing, or a call do NOT waive qualification.
+Ask at least TWO useful diagnostic questions, one at a time, and understand both
+answers. A name, contact field, greeting, or offer request does not count.
+
+QUESTION 1 (only if they haven't said what they need):
+"What do you need help with — a service, a general question, or something else?"
+[[CHIPS: "I want to discuss a service", "I have a general question", "Something else"]]
+
+QUESTION 2 (only if they picked "a service" AND haven't said which):
+"Which service, and what's the main result you're hoping for?"
+
+AFTER QUALIFICATION:
+- A specific operational need plus explicit call request → [[BOOK_CALL]]
+- A confirmed foundational need → [[PLAYBOOK]]
+- Unknown need → clarify, do not default to an offer.
+
+FORBIDDEN IN THIS SCOPE:
+- Naming a leak
+- Referencing their score, audit, or any past conversation
+- Inventing specifics about their business
+- Running a mini-consultation
+- Asking about brand assets, logos, or channels
+
+KEEP IT SHORT. One or two sentences, then a chip or a route tag.
+Example: "Got it — let's get you to the right person. What's the main
+result you're hoping for?" (then route based on the answer)
+`;
+
+    case STEPS.RE_VISIT_GREETING:
+      return `
+RETURNING USER. ${userName} is back. Don't restart. Ask what brought them back.
+[[CHIPS: "Following up on my review", "Ready to take action", "New question"]]`;
+
+    default:
+      return `
+UNMATCHED STEP "${step}". Acknowledge ${userName}, ask one clarifying question.`;
+  }
+}
+
+// ============================================================
+// HELPERS
+// ============================================================
+
+export function getFollowerBand(followerCount) {
+  if (followerCount === null || followerCount === undefined) return null;
+  if (followerCount < 500) return 'UNDER_500';
+  if (followerCount <= 1500) return '500_TO_1500';
+  return 'OVER_1500';
+}
+
+export function hasSignificantMismatch(extracted, stated) {
+  if (!extracted?.followers || !stated?.followers) return false;
+  const diff = Math.abs(extracted.followers - stated.followers);
+  return diff > extracted.followers * 0.2;
+}
+
+export function determineRoutingAction({
+  questionsAsked = 0, diagnosticAnswers = 0, problemType = 'unknown',
+  scope = 'audit', explicitCallRequested = false,
+}) {
+  if (questionsAsked < 2 || diagnosticAnswers < 2) return questionsAsked === 0 ? STEPS.AWAITING_DIAGNOSTIC_Q1 : STEPS.AWAITING_DIAGNOSTIC_Q2;
+  if (problemType === 'foundational') return STEPS.ROUTING_TO_PLAYBOOK;
+  if (problemType === 'operational' && (scope !== 'support' || explicitCallRequested)) return STEPS.ROUTING_TO_CALL;
+  return STEPS.AWAITING_DIAGNOSTIC_Q2;
+}
+
+export function buildAuditContextFromFormData(formData) {
+  return {
+    userName:  formData.fullName  || formData.name  || 'there',
+    brandName: formData.brandName || 'your brand',
+    entryPoint: 'AUDIT_FLOW',
+    auditData: {
+      currentStep:     STEPS.AWAITING_DIAGNOSTIC_Q1,
+      presenceType:    formData.platformType || formData.presenceType,
+      hasWebsite:      formData.platformType === 'website',
+      websiteUrl:      formData.websiteUrl   || null,
+      hasNoPresence:   formData.platformType === 'none',
+      platform:        formData.socialPlatform || null,
+      handle:          formData.socialLink     || null,
+      isReturningUser: formData.isReturningUser || false,
+    },
+  };
+}
diff --git a/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-request.ts b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-request.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..170ba97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-request.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+import { STEPS } from './haven-prompts.js';
+
+export class HavenRequestError extends Error {
+  constructor(message: string, public status = 400) { super(message); }
+}
+
+export const ALLOWED_ORIGINS = [
+  'https://themarketinghaven.xyz', 'https://www.themarketinghaven.xyz',
+  'http://localhost:5173', 'http://localhost:5175', 'http://localhost:3000',
+];
+
+export function responseHeaders(request: Request) {
+  const origin = request.headers.get('origin');
+  return {
+    'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Cache-Control': 'no-store', Vary: 'Origin',
+    'Access-Control-Allow-Headers': 'authorization, x-client-info, apikey, content-type',
+    'Access-Control-Allow-Methods': 'POST, OPTIONS',
+    ...(origin && ALLOWED_ORIGINS.includes(origin) ? { 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': origin } : {}),
+  };
+}
+
+export function verifyOrigin(request: Request) {
+  const origin = request.headers.get('origin');
+  if (origin && !ALLOWED_ORIGINS.includes(origin)) throw new HavenRequestError('Origin not allowed.', 403);
+}
+
+export async function readBoundedJson(request: Request, maxBytes = 8 * 1024 * 1024) {
+  if (Number(request.headers.get('content-length')) > maxBytes) throw new HavenRequestError('Request is too large.', 413);
+  const reader = request.body?.getReader();
+  if (!reader) throw new HavenRequestError('A JSON body is required.');
+  const decoder = new TextDecoder('utf-8', { fatal: true });
+  let size = 0, raw = '';
+  try {
+    while (true) {
+      const { value, done } = await reader.read();
+      if (done) break;
+      size += value.byteLength;
+      if (size > maxBytes) {
+        await reader.cancel();
+        throw new HavenRequestError('Request is too large.', 413);
+      }
+      raw += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
+    }
+    raw += decoder.decode();
+    const body = JSON.parse(raw);
+    if (!body || typeof body !== 'object' || Array.isArray(body)) throw new Error('Object required');
+    return body;
+  } catch (error) {
+    if (error instanceof HavenRequestError) throw error;
+    throw new HavenRequestError('Invalid JSON body.');
+  } finally { reader.releaseLock(); }
+}
+
+export function screenshotPart(screenshot: unknown) {
+  if (typeof screenshot !== 'string' || screenshot.length > 7 * 1024 * 1024) {
+    throw new HavenRequestError('Please upload a PNG, JPEG or WebP image smaller than 5 MB.', 413);
+  }
+  const match = screenshot.match(/^data:(image\/(?:png|jpeg|webp));base64,([A-Za-z0-9+/]+={0,2})$/);
+  if (!match || match[2].length % 4 !== 0) throw new HavenRequestError('Screenshot must be a PNG, JPEG or WebP data URL.');
+  const size = match[2].length * 3 / 4 - (match[2].endsWith('==') ? 2 : match[2].endsWith('=') ? 1 : 0);
+  if (size > 5 * 1024 * 1024) throw new HavenRequestError('Screenshot exceeds 5 MB.', 413);
+  return { inline_data: { mime_type: match[1], data: match[2] } };
+}
+
+export function textValue(value: unknown, max: number, fallback = '') {
+  return typeof value === 'string' ? value.slice(0, max).replace(/[\u0000-\u001f\u007f]/g, ' ').trim() : fallback;
+}
+
+export function validateChatBody(body: Record<string, unknown>) {
+  if ('systemPrompt' in body) throw new HavenRequestError('Browser-provided system instructions are not accepted.');
+  const scope = body.scope || 'support';
+  if (!['audit', 'support', 'service'].includes(String(scope))) throw new HavenRequestError('Invalid conversation scope.');
+  const context = body.context || {};
+  if (typeof context !== 'object' || Array.isArray(context)) throw new HavenRequestError('Invalid conversation context.');
+  if ('systemPrompt' in context) throw new HavenRequestError('Browser-provided system instructions are not accepted.');
+  if (!Array.isArray(body.messages) || body.messages.length === 0 || body.messages.length > 40) {
+    throw new HavenRequestError('Send between 1 and 40 conversation messages.');
+  }
+  let total = 0;
+  const messages = body.messages.map((item) => {
+    if (!item || !['user', 'agent'].includes(item.role) || typeof item.content !== 'string' || item.content.length > 4000) {
+      throw new HavenRequestError('Messages must contain a user or agent role and at most 4000 characters.');
+    }
+    total += item.content.length;
+    return { role: item.role as 'user' | 'agent', content: item.content };
+  });
+  if (total > 24000 || messages[messages.length - 1].role !== 'user') {
+    throw new HavenRequestError('Conversation history is too long or does not end with your message.');
+  }
+  const screenshot = body.screenshot || null;
+  if (screenshot) screenshotPart(screenshot);
+  if (!messages[messages.length - 1].content.trim() && !screenshot) throw new HavenRequestError('A message or screenshot is required.');
+  return { scope: scope as 'audit' | 'support' | 'service', context: context as Record<string, unknown>, messages, screenshot: screenshot as string | null };
+}
+
+export function savedStep(value: unknown) {
+  return Object.values(STEPS).includes(value as string) && value !== STEPS.GREETING
+    ? value as string : STEPS.AWAITING_DIAGNOSTIC_Q1;
+}
diff --git a/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-routing.js b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-routing.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4ad17f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-routing.js
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+const SERVICE_QUESTIONS = {
+  web: 'In Brand & Web Engineering, which part of your website are you looking to improve, and what is going wrong there?',
+  growth: 'In Strategic Growth, what are you trying to grow, and where is progress getting stuck?',
+  content: 'In Content & Social, who are you trying to reach, and what is your content struggling to achieve?',
+};
+
+export function gateHavenRouting(rawText, context = {}) {
+  const text = typeof rawText === 'string' ? rawText : '';
+  const hasCall = /\[\[(?:BOOK_CALL|STEP:ROUTING_TO_CALL)\]\]|https?:\/\/(?:www\.)?calendly\.com\/|\b(?:book|schedule|arrange|recommend|suggest|hop|jump|join|next step)\b[^.!?\n]{0,60}\b(?:strategy )?call\b|\b(?:strategy|discovery) call\b[^.!?\n]{0,35}\b(?:would|could|will|can) help\b/i.test(text);
+  const hasBook = /\[\[(?:PLAYBOOK|STEP:ROUTING_TO_PLAYBOOK)\]\]|https?:\/\/(?:www\.)?themarketinghaven\.xyz\/?(?:#shop|shop)|\b(?:buy|purchase|grab|recommend|suggest|start with)\b[^.!?\n]{0,60}\b(?:unseen )?playbook\b|\bplaybook\b[^.!?\n]{0,40}\b(?:right|best|next) (?:step|move|choice)\b/i.test(text);
+  if (!hasCall && !hasBook) return text;
+  if (/\b(?:let me think|not ready|rather not|don['’]?t want|do not want)\b/i.test(String(context.latestUserText || ''))) {
+    return 'Of course. Take your time. You can come back to this conversation when you are ready.';
+  }
+  const qualified = Number(context.questionsAsked) >= 2 && Number(context.diagnosticAnswers) >= 2;
+  const question = Number(context.questionsAsked) === 0
+    ? SERVICE_QUESTIONS[context.serviceId] || 'What are you building, who is it for, and what is the main problem you want to solve?'
+    : 'What have you already tried, and where does the process stop working?';
+  if (!qualified) return `${question}\n[[DIAGNOSTIC_QUESTION]]`;
+  const marker = text.match(/\[\[NEED:(FOUNDATIONAL|OPERATIONAL|UNKNOWN)\]\]/)?.[1]?.toLowerCase();
+  let problem = context.problemType || marker || 'unknown';
+  if (problem === 'unknown') {
+    const latest = String(context.latestUserText || '');
+    if (/\b(?:broken|crash(?:ing|es)?|not loading|payment fail(?:ing|ure)?|checkout fail(?:ing|ure)?|website (?:repair|rebuild)|implement|integration|tracking (?:setup|broken))\b/i.test(latest)) problem = 'operational';
+    else if (/\b(?:positioning|clarity|unclear (?:offer|audience)|content direction|brand message|build(?:ing)? trust)\b/i.test(latest)) problem = 'foundational';
+  }
+  if (problem === 'foundational') {
+    if (hasCall) return 'The gap we have identified is in clarity, positioning, or trust. The Unseen Playbook gives you a strategic foundation to work through it at your own pace.\n[[PLAYBOOK]]\n[[NEED:FOUNDATIONAL]]';
+    return text.replace(/\[\[BOOK_CALL\]\]/g, '');
+  }
+  if (problem === 'operational' && hasCall && !(context.scope === 'support' && context.explicitCallRequested !== true)) {
+    return text.replace(/\[\[PLAYBOOK\]\]/g, '');
+  }
+  if (context.scope === 'support' && problem === 'operational' && context.explicitCallRequested !== true) {
+    return 'This sounds like an execution issue rather than a missing marketing foundation. Which exact step is failing so we can understand the right kind of help?\n[[DIAGNOSTIC_QUESTION]]';
+  }
+  return 'Before I recommend anything, is the main gap explaining your value to customers, or getting a specific website, campaign, or system to work?\n[[DIAGNOSTIC_QUESTION]]';
+}
diff --git a/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-scoring.ts b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-scoring.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ff3422
--- /dev/null
+++ b/supabase/functions/_shared/haven-scoring.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+import { HavenRequestError } from './haven-request.ts';
+
+export const MAX_SUMMARY_CHARS = 6000;
+export type ScoringResult = {
+  state: 'valid' | 'bad_data'; score: number | null;
+  breakdown: Record<string, number> | null; biggestIssue: string | null;
+};
+
+export function normalizeWebsiteUrl(raw: unknown) {
+  if (typeof raw !== 'string' || raw.length > 2048) throw new HavenRequestError('A valid website URL is required.');
+  let url: URL;
+  try { url = new URL(/^https?:\/\//i.test(raw.trim()) ? raw.trim() : `https://${raw.trim()}`); }
+  catch { throw new HavenRequestError('A valid website URL is required.'); }
+  const host = url.hostname.toLowerCase();
+  if (!['https:', 'http:'].includes(url.protocol) || url.username || url.password
+    || (url.port && !['80', '443'].includes(url.port))
+    || !host.includes('.') || /(?:^|\.)(?:localhost|local|internal)$/.test(host)
+    || /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/.test(host) || host.includes(':')
+    || /[\u0000-\u0020]/.test(raw)) {
+    throw new HavenRequestError('Please provide a public website URL.');
+  }
+  url.hash = '';
+  return url.toString();
+}
+
+export function extractWebsiteText(raw: string) {
+  const markdown = raw.includes('Markdown Content:') ? raw.slice(raw.indexOf('Markdown Content:') + 17) : raw;
+  const content = markdown.replace(/!\[[^\]]*\]\([^)]*\)/g, '')
+    .replace(/\[([^\]]+)\]\([^)]*\)/g, '$1').replace(/https?:\/\/\S+/g, '')
+    .replace(/[ \t]+/g, ' ').replace(/\n{3,}/g, '\n\n').trim();
+  return content.slice(0, MAX_SUMMARY_CHARS);
+}
+
+export function hasMeaningfulBusinessText(summary: string) {
+  const words = summary.toLowerCase().match(/[\p{L}][\p{L}'’-]*/gu) || [];
+  const unique = new Set(words);
+  if (summary.length < 300 || words.length < 45 || unique.size < 25) return false;
+  const legalTerms = words.filter((word) => /^(privacy|cookie|cookies|consent|copyright|liability|jurisdiction|legal|rights|licence|license|gdpr|agreement|terms|conditions)$/.test(word)).length;
+  const lines = summary.split('\n').map((line) => line.trim()).filter(Boolean);
+  const legalLines = lines.filter((line) => /privacy|cookie|terms of|all rights reserved|liability|jurisdiction|personal data|governing law/i.test(line));
+  const legalChars = legalLines.reduce((total, line) => total + line.length, 0);
+  return legalTerms / words.length < 0.12 && legalChars / summary.length < 0.65;
+}
+
+export function parseScoringResult(raw: string, kind: 'website' | 'social'): ScoringResult | null {
+  try {
+    const cleaned = raw.trim().replace(/^```(?:json)?\s*/i, '').replace(/\s*```$/, '');
+    const value = JSON.parse(cleaned);
+    if (value.state === 'bad_data') return { state: 'bad_data', score: null, breakdown: null, biggestIssue: null };
+    if (value.state !== 'valid' || !Number.isInteger(value.score) || value.score < 0 || value.score > 100) return null;
+    const keys = kind === 'website' ? ['clarity', 'trust', 'conversion', 'technical', 'content']
+      : ['profile', 'consistency', 'engagement', 'readiness'];
+    const max = kind === 'website' ? 20 : 25;
+    if (!value.breakdown || keys.some((key) => !Number.isInteger(value.breakdown[key]) || value.breakdown[key] < 0 || value.breakdown[key] > max)) return null;
+    const breakdown = Object.fromEntries(keys.map((key) => [key, value.breakdown[key]]));
+    if (Object.values(breakdown).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) !== value.score) return null;
+    if (typeof value.biggestIssue !== 'string' || !value.biggestIssue.trim() || value.biggestIssue.length > 600) return null;
+    return { state: 'valid', score: value.score, breakdown, biggestIssue: value.biggestIssue.trim() };
+  } catch { return null; }
+}
+
+export async function persistScoring(supabase: any, reviewId: string, result: ScoringResult | { state: 'failed' }, summary: string | null) {
+  const valid = result.state === 'valid' ? result as ScoringResult : null;
+  const { error } = await supabase.from('brand_reviews').update({
+    scrape_state: result.state, scraped_summary: summary,
+    haven_score: valid?.score ?? null, score_breakdown: valid?.breakdown ?? null,
+    biggest_leak: valid?.biggestIssue ?? null, score_observed_at: new Date().toISOString(),
+  }).eq('id', reviewId).select('id').single();
+  if (error) throw new HavenRequestError('Could not save your review result. Please try again.', 500);
+}
+
+export function cachedScoring(review: Record<string, any>, kind: 'website' | 'social') {
+  const observed = new Date(review.score_observed_at).getTime();
+  if (!Number.isFinite(observed) || Date.now() - observed >= 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000) return null;
+  if (review.scrape_state === 'bad_data') return { state: 'bad_data' as const, score: null, breakdown: null, biggestIssue: null };
+  return parseScoringResult(JSON.stringify({ state: review.scrape_state, score: review.haven_score,
+    breakdown: review.score_breakdown, biggestIssue: review.biggest_leak }), kind);
+}
diff --git a/supabase/functions/_shared/review-access.ts b/supabase/functions/_shared/review-access.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0c1eef0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/supabase/functions/_shared/review-access.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+// A private bearer capability binds a visitor to one saved review and audit session.
+// Only its SHA-256 digest is stored; never include the token or digest in logs/API lists.
+export class ReviewAccessError extends Error {
+  constructor(message: string, public status = 403) { super(message); }
+}
+
+export async function hashReviewToken(token: string): Promise<string> {
+  const digest = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', new TextEncoder().encode(token));
+  return Array.from(new Uint8Array(digest), (byte) => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
+}
+
+export function validReviewCredentials(sessionId: unknown, reviewId: unknown, token: unknown): boolean {
+  const uuid = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;
+  return typeof sessionId === 'string' && uuid.test(sessionId)
+    && typeof reviewId === 'string' && uuid.test(reviewId)
+    && typeof token === 'string' && /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/i.test(token);
+}
+
+function equalDigest(a: string, b: string) {
+  if (a.length !== b.length) return false;
+  let difference = 0;
+  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) difference |= a.charCodeAt(i) ^ b.charCodeAt(i);
+  return difference === 0;
+}
+
+export async function verifyReviewAccess(supabase: any, sessionId: unknown, reviewId: unknown, accessToken: unknown) {
+  if (!validReviewCredentials(sessionId, reviewId, accessToken)) {
+    throw new ReviewAccessError('Review access credentials are required.', 403);
+  }
+  const { data: session, error: sessionError } = await supabase.from('haven_sessions')
+    .select('id, review_id, scope, current_step, last_step_reached').eq('id', sessionId).maybeSingle();
+  if (sessionError) throw new ReviewAccessError('Unable to verify the saved session.', 500);
+  if (!session || session.scope !== 'audit' || session.review_id !== reviewId) {
+    throw new ReviewAccessError('Review access denied.');
+  }
+  const { data: proof, error: proofError } = await supabase.from('review_access_tokens')
+    .select('token_hash').eq('review_id', reviewId).eq('session_id', sessionId).maybeSingle();
+  if (proofError) throw new ReviewAccessError('Unable to verify review access.', 500);
+  if (!proof || !equalDigest(proof.token_hash, await hashReviewToken(accessToken as string))) {
+    throw new ReviewAccessError('Review access denied.');
+  }
+  const { data: review, error: reviewError } = await supabase.from('brand_reviews')
+    .select('*').eq('id', reviewId).maybeSingle();
+  if (reviewError) throw new ReviewAccessError('Unable to read the saved review.', 500);
+  if (!review) throw new ReviewAccessError('Review access denied.');
+  return { session, review };
+}
diff --git a/supabase/functions/admin-retry-purchase-email/index.ts b/supabase/functions/admin-retry-purchase-email/index.ts
